  "instructions": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a large pot over medium heat. Add the onion and carrots and cook for 6 minutes, stirring often, until soft.",
    "Stir in the garlic and cook for 1 minute until fragrant.",
    "Add the diced tomatoes with their juice, the beans, the broth, the Italian seasoning, the salt, and the pepper. Bring to a boil.",
    "Mash about 1/2 cup of the beans against the side of the pot with a spoon. This thickens the soup.",
    "Stir in the pasta. Reduce to a steady simmer and cook for 10 to 12 minutes, stirring often, until the pasta is tender.",
    "Taste and add a pinch more salt if needed. The soup should be thick; if it is too thick, stir in a splash of water.",
    "Rest for 5 minutes before serving. The pasta will keep absorbing liquid, so add a little water when reheating leftovers."
  ],
